WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.152
Two hundred and seventy-six million dollars.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:07.602
That is how much Canadian charities sent to Israel in 2024.

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:11.363
The five-year total exceeds one point three billion dollars.

00:00:11.363 --> 00:00:17.886
Twelve organizations have had their charitable status revoked by the Canada Revenue Agency for improper use of funds.

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:22.920
The pipeline includes organizations directly connected to the Israeli Defence Forces.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.613
These donations are tax-deductible.

00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:30.181
Canadian taxpayers subsidize the transfer through charitable tax credits.

00:00:30.181 --> 00:00:35.011
Military recruitment through Canadian charitable organizations has been documented.

00:00:35.011 --> 00:00:42.874
The money flows through registered charities, arrives in Israel, and funds activities that would be illegal if conducted by the Canadian government directly.

00:00:42.874 --> 00:00:49.420
The charity pipeline is the policy the government cannot publicly defend — so it outsources it to the non-profit sector.
